      "body": "## Motivation\r\n\r\nDispatch in `dsv4_attn_metadata_kernels.py` is keyed on `value.is_cuda`, so XPU\r\ninputs fall through to the torch reference. The reference is not numerically\r\nequivalent to the triton kernel it stands in for. In\r\n`build_causal_swa_page_indices` the reference indexes `full_to_swa_mapping` with\r\n-1, and torch wraps that to the last table entry, while the kernel stores the -1\r\nsentinel. A wrapped index reads a real page instead of being treated as absent.\r\n\r\nThis is a correctness fix, not a performance change.\r\n\r\n## Modifications\r\n\r\n`_inputs_on_cuda` becomes `_inputs_on_accelerator` and answers true for XPU as\r\nwell, so `BuildPageTablePositions` and `BuildCausalSwaPageIndices` take the\r\ntriton arm there. The rename keeps the name honest now that it covers more than\r\nCUDA; it is module-private with three call sites.\r\n\r\n`ExpandPrefillCausally` is the exception and does not consult that helper on XPU.\r\nIts triton kernel does not compile under triton-xpu 3.7.2, so a new `xpu`\r\nclassmethod calls the native `dsv4_expand_prefill_causally_out` op. Outputs are\r\ncaller-allocated at the padded width, which is what graph capture at a fixed\r\nwidth needs.\r\n\r\nCUDA and CPU behaviour is unchanged on every path.\r\n\r\n## Accuracy Tests\r\n\r\nThe op this dispatches to is covered by `tests/test_dsv4_attn_metadata.py` in\r\nsgl-kernel-xpu, which checks it against a Python reference across batch and\r\nsequence-length grids, the padding tail, an empty batch, two negative controls\r\nand graph replay.\r\n\r\nHappy to add a dispatch-level unit test under `test/registered/xpu/` if you would\r\nlike the routing itself pinned, alongside the existing\r\n`test_intel_xpu_linear_attn_dispatch.py`.\r\n\r\n## Benchmarking and Profiling\r\n\r\nNone. This corrects which arm XPU takes; it is not a performance change.\r\n\r\n## Dependency\r\n\r\nNeeds `dsv4_expand_prefill_causally_out` in sgl-kernel-xpu, which is\r\nsgl-project/sgl-kernel-xpu#505. Kept as a draft until that lands.\r\n\r\n---",
